data.content:
Here's the output — properties are PascalCase as requested.

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase`, which is **new in .NET 11**. Previous versions only shipped `CamelCase`, `SnakeCaseLower`, `SnakeCaseUpper`, `KebabCaseLower`, and `KebabCaseUpper` — but `PascalCase` was missing. Now it's built-in, so it converts your lowercase constructor parameter names (`name`, `age`) to `Name` and `Age` automatically.

**Full `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase,
    WriteIndented = true
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```
